    "body": "UI/UX pre-check of head `3d7587869`, from sn3ro (Claude Code), the UI/UX reviewer of the plan #4245. This is a contributor's pre-check, not a collaborator review. It does not change the quick pass of qsmits.\n\n## What I ran\n\n- A local build of `3d7587869` (detached worktree, no change pushed).\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib -- command_table`: 8 passed, 0 failed.\n- Local screenshots at 1366 × 768 from `ShellUi::seeded()`, each menu open (a temporary `#[ignore]` test that I did not push).\n\n![the six menus](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4490-review/menus-grid.png)\n\n## What is good\n\n- One table for the ribbon, the menu and the keys is the right base for D and for a later command search.\n- The Operation menu with one submenu for each section reads well. The disabled kinds (Chamfer, Thread, Undercut, V-Carve) show as disabled, with a reason on hover.\n- The shortcut hints are in the rows and follow the platform (`Cmd` on macOS).\n- The AccessKit names (\"View menu\", the row label without the shortcut) are clean.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **View ▸ Panels and View ▸ Theme open a drop-down far from the menu.** A click on View ▸ Panels closes the menu and opens the ribbon's Panels drop-down under the ribbon cell, at x ≈ 1100. The click was at x ≈ 260 (top image below). The user must find the list about 850 px away. Theme does the same.\n\n   ![View > Panels, and Operation > Milling 2D](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sn3ro/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/4490-review/panels-op.png)\n\n   Proposal: make Panels and Theme submenus of View, with the same rows as the ribbon lists (the pane check boxes, \"Panel setups…\", \"Reset layout\"; the themes and the colour-vision rows). The body of #4245 also names \"View ▸ Reset layout\" as the way to open all panes again (PR P), so a user looks for it directly in the View menu.\n\n2. **The rows that open a dialog have no \"…\".** The desktop convention is that a menu row which opens a dialog ends with \"…\", and a row that acts at once does not. The menu uses the ribbon words as they are: \"Model\", \"Open\", \"Save As\", \"Post\". Only \"Panel setups…\" (in the ribbon list) has it. `Row` already has its own `label` field, but `item` reads `text_of(c, state)`, the ribbon caption. Proposal: menu labels from the table, for example \"Import model…\", \"Open…\", \"Save As…\", \"Post…\". The ribbon keeps its short captions.\n\n3. **The menus have no groups.** File lists New, Model, Open, Save, Save As, Post and Quit with no separator, and \"Model\" (an import) stands between New and Open. Proposal:\n   - File: New, Open… | Save, Save As… | Import model… | Post… | Quit;\n   - Edit: Undo, Redo | Copy, Paste, Delete.\n\n   A `group` field in the table row (or a separator row) keeps this in the one table.\n\n4. **A question on one word.** The Operation menu says \"Run\", as the ribbon does. The mockup E1 and the status words of #4245 say \"Generate\" (\"Needs regenerate\"). If the plan uses \"Generate\", this PR is a good place for the menu to use it. If \"Run\" stays, no change is needed. This is a question, not a defect.\n\n## Not checked\n\n- The light theme.\n- A key press for each row. The table tests check the key map; I did not press the keys.\n- macOS (the `Cmd` hint is read from the code only).\n\nFindings 1 to 3 are menu text and structure. They change no command and no test of the ribbon.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
